# Vesuva enters as a copy of Bot2's Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth (CR 707.2): the copy has Urborg's name, legendary supertype and
# "Each land is a Swamp in addition to its other land types". Before Blood Moon every land is a Swamp. Then Blood Moon:
# both Urborgs are nonbasic lands it makes Mountains, and each loses the abilities its rules text and its copy effect gave it
# (CR 305.7: "any copiable effects affecting that land"; KI-51), so the Swamp-making abilities are gone - they depend on
# Blood Moon, which changes their existence, and wait for it (CR 613.8a-b) - and no land is a Swamp. The copy effect
# itself stays: Vesuva is still a legendary Land - Mountain named Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Vesuva
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Blood Moon
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth
Island x30

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Vesuva.Play
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Subtypes = Mountain; Swamp
? Bot1.Battlefield.Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth.Subtypes = Swamp
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
? Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Subtypes = Island; Swamp
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Blood Moon.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate(Ability: Add {R})
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth.Subtypes = Mountain
Bot1.Battlefield.Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth.Supertypes = Legendary
Bot2.Battlefield.Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth.Subtypes = Mountain
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Subtypes = Mountain
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Subtypes = Island
